{"id":"obesity","cards":[{"id":"obesit460ab878","l":1,"f":"<b>18.5–24.9</b> — Class?","b":"Normal","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesit5b482e57","l":1,"f":"<b>25–29.9</b> — Class?","b":"<b>Overweight</b>","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesitb80c9633","l":1,"f":"<b>30–34.9</b> — Class?","b":"<b>Obesity grade I</b>","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesitbfaac9b3","l":1,"f":"<b>35–39.9</b> — Class?","b":"<b>Obesity grade II</b>","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesit054401e5","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 40</b> — Class?","b":"<b>Grade III — severe / morbid</b>","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesit691ac8f5","l":2,"f":"Group with the highest prevalence of obesity worldwide","b":"keyed <b>Western low socioeconomic</b> groups","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesit253f4cf1","l":2,"f":"Basal metabolic rate of an obese person vs a normal-weight person of the same age and sex","b":"<b>more</b> (a larger body has more lean and fat mass to maintain)","c":"The big picture"},{"id":"obesit062e8692","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 40</b> — Surgery indicated when?","b":"<b>Always</b>","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesit796652d1","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 40</b> — Notes?","b":"Even <b>without</b> comorbidities","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesite785b28b","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 35</b> — Surgery indicated when?","b":"<b>+ obesity-related comorbidity</b>","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesit22a38210","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 35</b> — Notes?","b":"<b>T2DM, hypertension, dyslipidaemia, OSA</b>","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesita1ab771c","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 30</b> — Surgery indicated when?","b":"Can be considered <b>+ metabolic disease</b>","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesit4351ec23","l":1,"f":"<b>≥ 30</b> — Notes?","b":"Especially <b>uncontrolled T2DM</b> (updated <b>ASMBS</b>)","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesit262b3036","l":2,"f":"Work-up of an obese patient is directed towards","b":"<b>comorbidities</b>","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesit2f1890c0","l":2,"f":"RYGB is indicated for which comorbidity","b":"<b>diabetes mellitus</b> (best metabolic effect)","c":"Indications"},{"id":"obesit851b07e3","l":1,"f":"<b>Severe / high-grade oesophagitis</b> — Rules out?","b":"<b>Sleeve (LSG)</b>","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit5f0d1175","l":1,"f":"<b>Severe / high-grade oesophagitis</b> — Key point?","b":"Not a contraindication to all bariatric surgery","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit27bd67b0","l":1,"f":"<b>GERD</b> — Rules out?","b":"<b>Not absolute</b>","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit913c1f63","l":1,"f":"<b>GERD</b> — Key point?","b":"Obesity + significant reflux → often a better candidate for <b>RYGB</b>","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit45523799","l":1,"f":"<b>Unfit for anaesthesia/surgery</b> — Rules out?","b":"All bariatric surgery","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit1fe5c40b","l":1,"f":"<b>Unfit for anaesthesia/surgery</b> — Key point?","b":"Any condition preventing safe GA or surgery","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit1017758c","l":1,"f":"<b>Pregnancy</b> — Rules out?","b":"All bariatric surgery","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesit1f522a17","l":1,"f":"<b>Pregnancy</b> — Key point?","b":"General contraindication","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesitb0f42170","l":2,"f":"Absolute contraindication to bariatric surgery","b":"keyed <b>psychological disturbances</b> (untreated psychiatric illness, e.g. binge eating, substance abuse)","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesitba5fc052","l":2,"f":"Healthy woman, failed supervised programmes, <b>GERD with oesophagitis on PPIs</b>","b":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass</b>","c":"Contraindications"},{"id":"obesitc2e8d61b","l":1,"f":"<b>Sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b> — How common?","b":"<b>Most commonly performed</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesitcee5dce0","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — How common?","b":"Less often","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit70c4f8c0","l":1,"f":"<b>Sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Primarily restrictive</b> (↓ capacity → ↓ intake); some metabolic effects","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit5c7ea6bf","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Restriction + malabsorption</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesitc7afcab3","l":1,"f":"<b>Sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b> — Restrictive part?","b":"Stomach stapled along a <b>bougie-calibrated</b> sleeve; the rest removed","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit0f44a5b9","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — Restrictive part?","b":"<b>Small proximal gastric pouch</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit14760978","l":1,"f":"<b>Sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b> — Malabsorption?","b":"Minimal","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit8ef078c4","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — Malabsorption?","b":"Greater — bypassed small bowel","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit8cb23f00","l":1,"f":"<b>Sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b> — Reflux / oesophagitis?","b":"<b>Severe oesophagitis = contraindication</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit060cb85f","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — Reflux / oesophagitis?","b":"<b>Preferred with significant GERD</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesitd5d61fb4","l":1,"f":"<b>Sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b> — Nutritional deficiencies?","b":"Less common","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesitd2fe59ac","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — Nutritional deficiencies?","b":"<b>More common</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit187619f6","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b> — Internal hernia?","b":"<b>Particularly after bypass</b> — generally needs surgery","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit4c2a1dbd","l":1,"f":"<b>RYGB anatomy (lecture)</b>?","b":"small gastric pouch → <b>alimentary (Roux) limb ≈ 100 cm</b> carries food; <b>biliopancreatic limb ≈ 150 cm</b> carries secretions; they meet in the <b>common channel</b> (digestion &amp; absorption).","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesit3b677897","l":2,"f":"Sleeve 3 years ago with weight regain (BMI 40 → 48), <b>mid-sleeve stricture, dilated fundus and severe GERD</b>","b":"<b>convert to Roux-en-Y gastric bypass</b>","c":"Sleeve vs bypass"},{"id":"obesita316fb09","l":1,"f":"<b>Labs + nutritional assessment</b> — When?","b":"All patients","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesitfd654da4","l":1,"f":"<b>Labs + nutritional assessment</b> — Purpose?","b":"Baseline metabolic and nutritional status","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit6a650308","l":1,"f":"<b>ECG + chest X-ray</b> — When?","b":"Routine (lecture)","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit6796c3b3","l":1,"f":"<b>ECG + chest X-ray</b> — Purpose?","b":"Standard pre-op work-up","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit75e815a1","l":1,"f":"<b>Investigation EGD</b> — When?","b":"<b>GERD / reflux symptoms</b>","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesitf98deb78","l":1,"f":"<b>Investigation EGD</b> — Purpose?","b":"Severe oesophagitis changes the operation","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesitaaac9edf","l":1,"f":"<b>Abdominal US</b> — When?","b":"<b>Biliary colic</b> (RUQ pain after fatty meals ± right shoulder)","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit07688eb8","l":1,"f":"<b>Abdominal US</b> — Purpose?","b":"Gallstones","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit3f2ee189","l":1,"f":"<b>Upper GI contrast / barium swallow</b> — When?","b":"<b>Revisional surgery</b>","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit4872da08","l":1,"f":"<b>Upper GI contrast / barium swallow</b> — Purpose?","b":"Anatomy left by the previous operation","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesit4bbe586e","l":2,"f":"Why obese patients have more surgical complications","b":"keyed \"<b>procedures could take a longer time</b>\"","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesitb0bb5543","l":2,"f":"In morbid obesity, all are complications of OSA <b>except</b>","b":"<b>hypocarbia</b> (OSA causes <b>hypercarbia</b>, hypoxia and right heart failure)","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesitcb9c61d7","l":2,"f":"Obese 40-year-old rated low-to-intermediate risk for day surgery","b":"because of <b>BMI 32.2</b>","c":"Pre-operative assessment"},{"id":"obesitc9d7c1e9","l":1,"f":"<b>Prophylaxis VTE</b> — Agent?","b":"<b>Enoxaparin</b>","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesitd4d3b84f","l":1,"f":"<b>Prophylaxis VTE</b> — Lower BMI?","b":"<b>40 mg if BMI &lt; 50</b>","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesit0f25f5d1","l":1,"f":"<b>Prophylaxis VTE</b> — Higher BMI?","b":"<b>60 mg if BMI ≥ 50</b>","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesit59607775","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical site infection</b> — Agent?","b":"<b>Cefazolin</b>","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesitff972f60","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical site infection</b> — Lower BMI?","b":"2 g","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesit8ed9d0b6","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical site infection</b> — Higher BMI?","b":"3 g","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesitc36c8c24","l":1,"f":"<b>Positioning</b>?","b":"intubate → <b>steep reverse Trendelenburg</b> (head up) → bowel falls inferiorly → exposes the stomach. Patients can slide — <b>foot support + straps</b>. <b>Drape from the nipples to the groin.</b>","c":"Intra-operative preparation"},{"id":"obesitc5af7902","l":1,"f":"<b>Early</b> — list them","b":"<b>DVT / PE</b> · <b>Staple-line leak</b> · Post-operative bleeding","c":"Complications"},{"id":"obesita27086b6","l":1,"f":"<b>Late</b> — list them","b":"<b>Internal hernia</b> — particularly after bypass; generally surgical · <b>Gallstones</b> — with rapid weight loss · <b>Nutritional deficiencies</b> — more after bypass than sleeve","c":"Complications"},{"id":"obesit9ade8f76","l":1,"f":"<b>Staple-line leak</b> — Haemodynamically stable?","b":"NPO · feeding tube nutrition · <b>IR drainage</b> of collections · endoscopic management","c":"Complications"},{"id":"obesit28ce7c50","l":1,"f":"<b>Staple-line leak</b> — Unstable?","b":"<b>Urgent operative exploration</b>","c":"Complications"},{"id":"obesita5b13d44","l":1,"f":"<b>Bleeding</b> — Haemodynamically stable?","b":"Conservative / observation","c":"Complications"},{"id":"obesitb8565db2","l":1,"f":"<b>Bleeding</b> — Unstable?","b":"Urgent intervention or surgery","c":"Complications"},{"id":"obesitbdbb5625","l":2,"f":"After sleeve: <b>tachycardia and falling urine output</b>","b":"<b>leak</b>","c":"Complications › Leak"},{"id":"obesit35bbaa5d","l":2,"f":"10 days after sleeve: <b>persistent hiccups</b>, HR 112, T 39 °C","b":"after resuscitation, <b>CT abdomen to rule out leak or abscess</b> (subphrenic collection irritates the diaphragm)","c":"Complications › Leak"},{"id":"obesit333e718c","l":2,"f":"Overt leak 1 week after sleeve, <b>unstable with peritonitis</b>","b":"after resuscitation, <b>surgical control of the leak, irrigation and drainage</b>","c":"Complications › Leak"},{"id":"obesita404d5a0","l":2,"f":"Gastric fistula of 250 mL/day 7 days after sleeve","b":"most associated with <b>hypokalaemia</b>","c":"Complications › Leak"},{"id":"obesit927aa4e9","l":2,"f":"2 months after gastric bypass with obstruction — most common cause besides adhesions","b":"<b>internal hernia</b>","c":"Complications › Obstruction, stricture & ulcer"},{"id":"obesit46773c45","l":2,"f":"4 years after RYGB, severe central colic, stable","b":"keyed <b>adhesions</b> (commonest cause of SBO overall; internal hernia is the key differential after RYGB)","c":"Complications › Obstruction, stricture & ulcer"},{"id":"obesit7bdd1e0f","l":2,"f":"5 weeks after bypass, <b>solids → then liquids</b> not tolerated","b":"<b>gastrojejunal stricture</b>","c":"Complications › Obstruction, stricture & ulcer"},{"id":"obesit6e414133","l":2,"f":"4 weeks after LRYGB, on-and-off severe epigastric pain with <b>blood-stained vomiting</b>, stable, soft abdomen","b":"<b>upper GI endoscopy</b> (marginal ulcer)","c":"Complications › Obstruction, stricture & ulcer"},{"id":"obesitd568f772","l":2,"f":"Marginal ulcer after Roux-en-Y — most common cause","b":"<b>NSAIDs</b>","c":"Complications › Obstruction, stricture & ulcer"},{"id":"obesit7de886b7","l":2,"f":"Complication of obesity surgery → <b>increased gallstone formation</b> (rapid weight loss","b":"more cholesterol in bile)","c":"Complications › Gallstones, deficiencies & SMA syndrome"},{"id":"obesit9fb7f7bd","l":2,"f":"3 years after sleeve: RUQ pain, jaundice, gallbladder stones and an 11-mm CBD","b":"<b>ERCP followed by cholecystectomy</b> (the papilla is still reachable after a sleeve, unlike after RYGB)","c":"Complications › Gallstones, deficiencies & SMA syndrome"},{"id":"obesitdb6c27e0","l":2,"f":"2 years after sleeve with <b>hyperparathyroidism</b>","b":"<b>vitamin D deficiency</b> (secondary hyperparathyroidism)","c":"Complications › Gallstones, deficiencies & SMA syndrome"},{"id":"obesit8417f360","l":2,"f":"Rapid weight loss on <b>Mounjaro (tirzepatide)</b>, abdominal distension relieved by vomiting","b":"<b>SMA syndrome</b> (third part of the duodenum compressed between the SMA and aorta)","c":"Complications › Gallstones, deficiencies & SMA syndrome"}]}